<title>DENMARK: Siemens, ABB win Danish rail order.</title>
<headline>Siemens, ABB win Danish rail order.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>German consortium Linke Hofmann Busch/Siemens and ABB -Mercedes Benz-owned AdTranz are to share an 8.2 billion Danish crown order from Danish State Railways, the Danish Transport Ministry said on Monday.  </p>
<p>A ministry spokesman said that the bulk of the order, for 112 commuter trains for a new Copenhagen transit system, estimated at around 6.0 billion crowns, would go to Linke Hofmann Busch/Siemens.</p>
<p>A sub-contract worth around 1.5 to 2.0 billion crowns would go to Danish AdTranz, formed on January 1, 1996, when Swedish-Swiss ABB and Germany's Daimler-Benz merged their locomotive manufacturing divisions, the spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Delivery was due to begin in 1999, culminating in 2005, he added.</p>
<p>-- Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33 969650</p>
